@ATTRS?{key=YES,equal=:,empty=no attributes}\n@
->Definition:
@SerialIOSimulationDefinition>@
#---
#---
;Disk1540Data
Id:@ID@(Size:@SIZE@)
@BYTES{blocksize=32,listsep=\,,tablesep=\ ,minsize=2}@
#@FBYTES{blocksize=32,listsep=\,,tablesep=\ ,minsize=2}@
#Include the command above to show all data when the size is bigger than 256 bytes...
#---
#---
;Disk1540Simulation
Id:@ID@
@ATTRS?{key=YES,equal=:,empty=no attributes}\n@
Device Number:@DEVICENUMBER@
->Data:
Name:@DATANAME@ (Size:@DATASIZE@)
@DATA?{fmter=Disk1540Data,empty=no data}\n---\n@
NOTE: Only the first 256 bytes are shown
NOTE: Change to FBYTES attribute in Disk1540Data structure instead
->Definition:
@SerialIOSimulationDefinition>@
#---
#---
;SerialPrinterSimulation
Id:@ID@
@ATTRS?{key=YES,equal=:,empty=no attributes}\n@
